    "The expected-cost decision is NOT uniformly better than argmax. Class weighting and a cost matrix encode the same asymmetry by two different mechanisms, and applying both double-counts it: with class_weight='balanced' the expected-cost rule degenerates to flagging every vehicle. Expected-cost decisions require CALIBRATED probabilities, and a class-weighted model's probabilities are not calibrated."
